==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|gŏn|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɒn/}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɒn|s=1}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɔːn/|a=AusE,archaic RP,MLE}}
* {{enPR|gôn|a=GenAm}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɔn/}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɔːn|s=1}}
* {{enPR|gŏn|a=cot-caught,traditional <<NYC>>}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɑn/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-gone.ogg|a=US|IPA=[ɡ̊ɑ̃ːn]}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɑːn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|gon}}, {{m|enm|igon}}, {{m|enm|gan}}, {{m|enm|ȝegan}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gān}}, {{m|ang|ġegān}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gānaz||gone}}, past participle of {{m|gem-pro|*gāną||to go}}. Cognate with West Germanic {{cog|sco|gane||gone}}, {{cog|fy|gien||gone}}, {{cog|nds|gahn||gone}}, and {{cog|nl|gegaan||gone}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form|cat2=irregular past participles}}

# {{inflection of|en|go||past|part}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|further,er}}

# [[away|Away]], having left.
#: {{ux|en|Are they '''gone''' already?}}
# No longer [[existing]], having [[passed]].
#: {{ux|en|The days of my youth are '''gone'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|All hopes for a truce are '''gone'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|All the little shops that used to be here are now '''gone'''.}}
# [[used up|Used up]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm afraid all the coffee is '''gone'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|If the milk is [[all gone|all '''gone''']], we'll drink our coffee black.}}
# Broken, failed.
#: {{ux|en|The bulb is '''gone'''. Can you put a new one in?}}
#: {{ux|en|The car isn't driveable — the steering is '''gone'''.}}
# [[dead|Dead]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=221|volume=I|passage=Dust, that a breath could blow aside, yet that was once, like ourselves, animate with hope, passion, and sorrow, is below; around are the vain memorials of human grief and human pride; yet all alike dedicated to the '''gone'''.}}
# [[doomed|Doomed]], [[done for]].
#: {{ux|en|Have you seen the company's revenue? It's [[through the floor]]. They're '''gone'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Not fully [[aware]] of one's surroundings, often through [[intoxication]] or mental [[decline]].
#: {{ux|en|Don't bother trying to understand what Grandma says; she's '''gone'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=28|passage=[S]he put on a kind of sing-song voice whenever she was pissed, it was one of the signs that she was really '''gone'''{{...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[infatuated|Infatuated]]; in love (+ {{m|en|on}}, {{m|en|for}}, {{m|en|in}}).
#* {{RQ:James Wings of the Dove|passage=I ''am'', of course, ‘'''gone'''’ for you.}}
#* {{RQ:Maugham Of Human Bondage|chapter=35
|passage=But he was pleased and happy and flattered. She was evidently frightfully '''gone''' on him.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|US|dated}} [[excellent|Excellent]], [[wonderful]]; [[crazy]].
#: {{ux|en|It was a group of real '''gone''' cats.}}
#* {{RQ:Kerouac On the Road|part=1|chapter=11|page=61|year_published=1976|passage=“All right, all right, don’t drop your gold all over the place. I have found the '''gonest''' little girl in the world and I am going straight to the Lion’s Den with her tonight.”}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[ago|Ago]] {{non-gloss|(used post-positionally)}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=w:George R.R. Martin|title=A Clash of Kings|page=491|publisher=Bantam|year_published=2011
|passage=Six nights '''gone''', your brother fell upon my uncle Stafford, encamped with his host at a village called Oxcross not three days ride from Casterly Rock.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} [[weak|Weak]]; [[faint]]; feeling a sense of [[goneness]].
# Of an arrow: [[wide of the mark]].
# {{non-gloss|Used with a duration to indicate for how long a process has been developing, an action has been performed or a state has persisted}}; ''especially'', [[pregnant]].
#: {{ux|en|She’s three months '''gone'''}}

